+Closes #614.
+
+## What this changes
+
+`/vision` can now run inside a **drive**. A drive is a run of plays that keeps going until its goal is met, then gets reviewed (ADR 029). This is item 5 of the #606 plan, one of the three pieces the Kickoff drive (#613) needs.
+
+- **Handed a drive's contract, `/vision` opens nothing.** It runs no `start-change`, and no commit, propose, review or merge of its own. It works on the drive's branch and still commits its model change there.
+- **It does not wait at its checkpoint.** It renders the checkpoint exactly as it would have been shown, then saves it, with the files it stands on, as a review record in the drive's review folder for the drive's end review.
+- **A question the drive did not answer still stops it.** With no intents and no goal, it asks the person. It never picks an answer itself (ADR 029: a new question stops the drive).
+- **Run by hand, nothing changes.**
+
+## Kapil's two choices (recorded in `.garura/project/issues/614/specs/plan.md`)
+
+1. **One shared drive contract.** A new rule, `standards/rules/drive-contract.md`, says what a drive hands a play. There is one shared checker (`check_drive_contract.py`) and one shared review-record writer (`write_drive_review.py`), canonical in `play-creator/references/` and stamped into `/vision`. `/intent` keeps its own check for now; `/understand` (#615) will use the shared one.
+2. **The checkpoint keeps learning from drives.** `gate_eval.py` takes a new answer, `deferred_to_drive_review`. `distill_gate_policy.py` skips it: it is not an approval and does not break a run of approvals, until the drive's review writes the person's real answer (that write-back is #617 / #613 work).
+
+## Where to look
+
+24 of the files are identical copies of two small edits to `gate_eval.py` and `distill_gate_policy.py`, one per play. Review the canonical copies in `core/components/plays/play-creator/references/`. The intent change went through `core/components/plays/vision/reference/ice.md` (C11, F12, F13, S7) and was recompiled; the fingerprint is refreshed.
+
+## Tests
+
+- All 21 test files under `core/` pass. New: `test_drive_contract.py` (14), plus 2 new cases in `test_gate_learning.py`.
+- `lint_play` passes on `/vision`.
+- All shared-script copies are byte-identical.
+
+## Not in this change
+
+- `/intent` moving to the shared contract checker.
+- The drive's review writing the person's real answer back into the checkpoint's learning record (#617 / #613).
